{"id":"aidisclose","name":"aidisclose","aliases":[],"caption":"Generate disclosure statements and checklists for the use of generative AI","authors":[{"id":"lourenco-j","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Joao M. Lourenco","year":"2025-2026"}],"license":"lppl1.3c","version":{"number":"1.12.0","date":"2026-02-21"},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      This package provides a standardized, transparent way\n      to declare the use of generative artificial intelligence\n      (AI) tools in academic, technical, and professional documents.\n      It implements an extension of the GAIDeT (Generative AI\n      Delegation Taxonomy), letting authors mark which tasks\n      were delegated to AI, list the tools used (or state that\n      none were), add optional numbered or unnumbered comments,\n      and automatically typeset a formatted disclosure section\n      or chapter with a task-based checklist.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      Configuration uses a key-value interface, and citations\n      for the taxonomy and the package can be managed automatically.\n      The package detects the document language through\n      <ref refid=\"babel\">babel<\u002fref> or\n      <ref refid=\"polyglossia\">polyglossia<\u002fref> and\n      ships translations for fourteen languages, falling back\n      to English.\n      A companion web generator/configurator is available at\n      <a href=\"https://aidisclose.org/\">https://aidisclose.org<\u002fref>.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/aidisclose/aidisclose-doc.pdf"},{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/aidisclose/README.md"}],"home":"https://aidisclose.org","repository":"https://github.com/joaomlourenco/aidisclose","ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/aidisclose","file":true},"miktex":"aidisclose","texlive":"aidisclose","topics":["form-fillin"]}